/-- If `f` vanishes on `Ici a`, then `deriv f` vanishes on all of `Ici a`.

For `x > a` the function `f` vanishes on the open neighbourhood `Ioi a` of `x`, hence
`deriv f x = 0` by eventual equality with the zero function; for `x = a` this is
`deriv_eq_zero_of_eqOn_Ici`. -/
